 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to designating a portion of the state highway system as the\n\"Putnam County Workers Memorial Bridge\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S8540",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8540-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Highways",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8540\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to designating a portion of the state highway system\nas the \"Putnam County Workers Memorial Bridge\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation would rename the Prospect Hill Road Bridge in the Town\nof Southeast, as the \"Putnam County Workers Memorial Bridge\" to honor\nthe men and women who work in Putnam County in the State of New York.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 designates the Prospect Hill Road Bridge located in the town\nof Southeast, Putnam County that crosses the Harlem Line tracks and\nparts of the MTA Metro-North Railroad's Brewster Yard as the \"Putnam\nCounty Workers Memorial Bridge\".\n\nSection 2 states that this act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe men and women within Putnam County work tirelessly to provide a\nlivelihood for their families and to contribute to their community.\nThese resolute citizens characterize a county that works together to\nsupport and maintain the area that they call home. Renaming the Prospect\nHill Road Bridge the \"Putnam County Workers Memorial Bridge\" serves to\nhonor these everyday men and women whose labor has had such an indelible\nimpact on our community.\n\nThe Prospect Hill Road Bridge is the ideal location to honor Putnam\nCounty workers for several reasons. The bridge, which is owned by the\nMTA, provides residents in the Town of Southeast and Village of Brewster\nwith direct access to the Metro North Southeast station, while also\neasing traffic in the area. Furthermore, the bridge was rebuilt in 2018.\n\nIt serves as a perfect example of the need to focus on improving our\nstate's infrastructure, while also highlighting the importance of the\nworkers we depend on to do the job.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nMinimal\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
